How it works
Wiz performs a deep fetch of the ServiceNow CMDB hierarchy. To ensure comprehensive coverage, Wiz targets primary CI (configuration item) tables and recursively includes all inherited subclasses. The fetch operation targets the following root tables and their children:
Computer—cmdb_ci_computer
Virtual Machine Instance—cmdb_ci_vm_instance
VMware Virtual Machine Instance—cmdb_ci_vmware_instance
Network gear—cmdb_ci_netgear
To see information about existing resources enriched with data fetched from ServiceNowCMDB:   Go to the Inventory > Imported Assets.  can filter Origin = ServiceNOW
The ServiceNow connector does not create new resources in Wiz. Instead, it enriches existing Wiz resources with additional metadata from ServiceNow CMDB. Therefore, assets appear on the Imported Assets page only if a matching resource already exists in Wiz and was successfully enriched. If no matching resources are found, no assets are displayed for Origin = ServiceNow.

